      "details": "The boot-config data buffer is freed if allocated, including after a read error that may follow allocation. The flash-access managed allocation is checked and freed in the same common cleanup. The two devm_kfree calls require a non-NULL managed device; otherwise devres retains the allocation until device teardown. Ghidra stock has the same two conditional frees. Static evidence did not establish that the device provider becomes unavailable during the operation, so this is a conditional retained-devres risk, not a confirmed runtime leak.",
